# Raw source bytes and downloaded portraits are the wave's EVIDENCE and are kept on disk for
# the length of the wave, not committed: they are large (29 MB across the two KS/KY directories)
# and every one of them is re-fetchable from a URL this wave recorded.
# A trailing comment on a pattern line is NOT a comment -- git reads the whole line, spaces and
# all, as the pattern. Keep every comment on its own line.
#
# What IS committed: the derived rosters, the portrait manifest -- which carries each portrait's
# source URL, byte count, dimensions and QA metrics -- and the district geometry.

# archived member pages and statute texts
*.html
member-pages/
statutes/
# meeting minutes and canvasses, cited by date in the rosters
*.pdf
*.docx
# downloaded portraits; every URL is in ks-portrait-manifest.json
portraits/
wichita-portraits/
sgco-headers/
# raw API and probe responses, named _<what-was-asked>
_*
